fence_manager: submit deferred work before waiting on pending fences

From Lichii PR 149, first commit (chuppatricky; open, not merged). The FSR3 commit of
that PR is left out.

With the split GPU thread, Scheduler::DeferFlush batches fence submissions for 500 us.
WaitPendingFences signals a fence and waits for it, but the command buffer that signals
it can still sit in that batch. The fencing thread then waits in WaitSubmitted for the
back thread, and the back thread is the one blocked here. Lichii saw this as a black
screen where Ocarina's intro hands over to gameplay.

Changed from the PR: FenceManager::SubmitDeferredWork flushes only on the split's back
thread. Only the back may submit (see InnerFence::Wait and Scheduler::DeferFlush), and
flush_pending is its own. On any other thread nothing was deferred by that thread and
the existing WaitSubmitted path asks the back to submit.

vk_fence_manager.cpp reaches the build as vk_fence_manager_cost.cpp; the one wait site
tools/prepare-vulkan-port.py counts there does not change.

diff --git a/src/video_core/fence_manager.h b/src/video_core/fence_manager.h
index d9f0ac2..8680adf 100644
--- a/src/video_core/fence_manager.h
+++ b/src/video_core/fence_manager.h
@@ -152,6 +152,11 @@ public:
                 wait_cv.notify_all();
             });
             SignalFence(std::move(func));
+            // The fence's commands can be held back by a deferred flush that only the split's
+            // back thread submits. The fencing thread waits for that submission before it
+            // releases the fence, so the back thread waiting here without submitting deadlocks
+            // (Ocarina of Time entering gameplay).
+            SubmitDeferredWork();
             std::unique_lock lk(wait_mutex);
             wait_cv.wait(
                 lk, [&wait_finished] { return wait_finished.load(std::memory_order_relaxed); });
@@ -187,6 +192,8 @@ protected:
     virtual bool IsFenceSignaled(TFence& fence) const = 0;
     /// Waits until a fence has been signalled by the host GPU.
     virtual void WaitFence(TFence& fence) = 0;
+    /// Submits work whose submission the backend deferred (called before blocking on a fence).
+    virtual void SubmitDeferredWork() {}
 
     VideoCore::RasterizerInterface& rasterizer;
     Tegra::GPU& gpu;
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_fence_manager.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_fence_manager.cpp
index b22bc32..925eed4 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_fence_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_fence_manager.cpp
@@ -74,4 +74,11 @@ void FenceManager::WaitFence(Fence& fence) {
     fence->Wait();
 }
 
+void FenceManager::SubmitDeferredWork() {
+    // Only the split's back thread defers flushes and may submit them (Scheduler::DeferFlush).
+    if (VideoCommon::GpuSplit::OnBackThread()) {
+        scheduler.FlushDeferred();
+    }
+}
+
 } // namespace Vulkan
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_fence_manager.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_fence_manager.h
index 3365735..606cfd6 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_fence_manager.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_fence_manager.h
@@ -62,6 +62,7 @@ protected:
     void QueueFence(Fence& fence) override;
     bool IsFenceSignaled(Fence& fence) const override;
     void WaitFence(Fence& fence) override;
+    void SubmitDeferredWork() override;
 
 private:
     Scheduler& scheduler;
